WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.802 --> 00:00:15.984
Tom stopped worrying about the murder because he had something else to worry about—Becky.

2
00:00:16.964 --> 00:00:19.164
She was sick, and Tom thought she might die.

3
00:00:20.125 --> 00:00:23.166
Tom was so worried about Becky that he stopped playing with his friends.

4
00:00:25.706 --> 00:00:28.907
One day Tom waited outside Becky's house, hoping to see her.

5
00:00:29.847 --> 00:00:32.048
When he didn't spot her at all, he was sad.

6
00:00:32.892 --> 00:00:34.613
Aunt Polly worried about Tom too.

7
00:00:35.413 --> 00:00:39.434
To make Tom feel better, she tried lots of new remedies that she read about in a women's

8
00:00:39.474 --> 00:00:43.955
magazine. One remedy was giving Tom a cold bath every evening.

9
00:00:45.596 --> 00:00:49.577
Afterward Aunt Polly would wrap him in many layers of blankets until he began to sweat.

10
00:00:50.477 --> 00:00:51.557
The treatment didn't help.

11
00:00:52.538 --> 00:00:54.418
It only made Tom quieter and sadder.

12
00:00:55.539 --> 00:01:00.060
Next Aunt Polly talked to her friends, and they recommended a medicine made from chili peppers.

13
00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:02.741
Aunt Polly decided to try it on Tom.

14
00:01:04.721 --> 00:01:07.562
She gave Tom a teaspoon of the medicine and watched his face.

15
00:01:11.403 --> 00:01:14.804
Tom's mouth, throat, and stomach felt as if they were on fire.

16
00:01:15.524 --> 00:01:17.385
He screamed and ran around the room.

17
00:01:18.285 --> 00:01:21.926
Aunt Polly was pleased because Tom was finally acting like himself again.

18
00:01:22.766 --> 00:01:26.507
She told Tom that if he didn't feel better tomorrow, she'd give him more medicine.

19
00:01:27.147 --> 00:01:29.148
Tom quickly decided to be less sad!

20
00:01:30.324 --> 00:01:32.266
Tom wondered what else the medicine could cure.

21
00:01:33.386 --> 00:01:35.848
The cat, for example, was suffering from laziness.

22
00:01:37.209 --> 00:01:41.372
The medicine had made Tom more active, so maybe it would make the cat more active too!

23
00:01:42.233 --> 00:01:44.794
Tom gave some hot chili pepper medicine to the cat.

24
00:01:46.536 --> 00:01:50.839
The cat leaped into the air, screamed, and ran around and around the room.

25
00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:54.501
He knocked over chairs, plants, and book shelves.

26
00:01:55.382 --> 00:01:57.564
Tom thought it was the funniest thing he had ever seen.

27
00:01:58.908 --> 00:02:01.951
Aunt Polly came into the room just as the cat jumped out the window.

28
00:02:01.971 --> 00:02:04.293
"What's wrong with the cat?"

29
00:02:04.833 --> 00:02:05.634
asked Aunt Polly.

30
00:02:06.975 --> 00:02:09.016
Tom was laughing too hard to answer.

31
00:02:09.997 --> 00:02:12.980
Aunt Polly saw the teaspoon and the medicine bottle on the floor.

32
00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:16.282
"How could you treat the cat like that?"

33
00:02:16.703 --> 00:02:17.724
she asked sternly.

34
00:02:18.524 --> 00:02:24.169
Tom said, "The cat's been lazy, and you don't love him enough, so I felt sorry for him.

35
00:02:25.190 --> 00:02:27.612
I decided to love the cat like you love me.

36
00:02:28.468 --> 00:02:29.809
I gave him some medicine."

37
00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:32.791
Tom's words made Aunt Polly feel bad.

38
00:02:33.692 --> 00:02:36.334
She hadn't meant to be unloving, so she apologized.

39
00:02:37.254 --> 00:02:39.656
She explained she only wanted Tom to feel better.

40
00:02:40.557 --> 00:02:44.640
Tom smiled and said, "I know you meant well, and it worked.

41
00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:47.422
I think the medicine helped the cat too.

42
00:02:48.342 --> 00:02:51.324
I've never seen him move so fast."

43
00:02:53.426 --> 00:02:58.129
Tom was still smiling about the cat when he got to school, but his amusement soon turned to

44
00:02:58.169 --> 00:03:00.331
delight. Becky was back!

45
00:03:01.292 --> 00:03:03.294
Tom tried everything to get Becky's attention.

46
00:03:04.295 --> 00:03:09.299
He jumped over the fence; he walked on his hands; he even did cartwheels off the school steps.

47
00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:13.843
But Becky was still mad about Tom being engaged to Amy first.

48
00:03:14.743 --> 00:03:20.828
Ignoring Tom, she turned to a friend and said loudly, "Some people think they're so smart, always showing

49
00:03:21.029 --> 00:03:24.732
off!" Tom was so angry that he ran into the woods.

50
00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:27.481
There he met his friend Joe Harper.

51
00:03:28.761 --> 00:03:29.742
Joe was angry too.

52
00:03:30.602 --> 00:03:33.023
His mother had punished him for something he didn't do.

53
00:03:34.604 --> 00:03:35.704
Tom had an idea.

54
00:03:35.724 --> 00:03:37.545
"Let's run away.

55
00:03:38.226 --> 00:03:39.686
That will make them sorry."

56
00:03:40.567 --> 00:03:43.048
Joe agreed and said he would like to live on an island.

57
00:03:44.008 --> 00:03:46.589
Tom and Joe were planning their new lives when they met Huck.

58
00:03:47.510 --> 00:03:49.671
Huck was also dissatisfied with his life.

59
00:03:50.571 --> 00:03:52.712
People didn't like him because his father was a drunk.

60
00:03:53.844 --> 00:03:55.666
Huck thought running away sounded fun.

61
00:03:56.687 --> 00:03:59.649
Huck helped Tom and Joe steal some food and find a log raft.

62
00:04:00.390 --> 00:04:04.673
Together they pushed the raft into the Mississippi River and headed for Jackson Island.

63
00:04:05.574 --> 00:04:07.796
Once on the island the boys became pirates.

64
00:04:09.137 --> 00:04:13.841
They took turns being their favorite pirate, and they had great battles on both land and sea.

65
00:04:13.861 --> 00:04:17.264
"Life as a pirate is great," said Huck.

66
00:04:17.284 --> 00:04:19.646
"I haven't had this much fun in ages."

67
00:04:20.647 --> 00:04:21.908
The other two boys agreed.

68
00:04:22.644 --> 00:04:25.206
"We should explore the island," said Joe.

69
00:04:25.226 --> 00:04:29.129
"We should look for buried treasure," shouted Tom.

70
00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:33.853
They spent the rest of the afternoon exploring the island and looking for buried treasure.

71
00:04:35.755 --> 00:04:39.958
Being a pirate was hard work, and by early evening they were tired and hungry.

72
00:04:39.978 --> 00:04:43.621
"It's time to build our camp," said Tom.

73
00:04:43.641 --> 00:04:48.725
"I think I saw some sailcloth snagged on a log," said Joe.

74
00:04:48.745 --> 00:04:51.868
"That will make an excellent tent," said Huck.

75
00:04:52.672 --> 00:04:57.119
They made a tent, cooked their food, talked around the fire, and went to sleep.
